      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): read app-server bindings from SQLite instead of retired JSON sidecar",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `live-codex-npm-plugin` release assertion still reads the retired `<sessionFile>.codex-app-server.json` sidecar after #101210 moved Codex app-server bindings into SQLite plugin state. The sidecar no longer exists on current main, so the assertion fails deterministically.\n\nCloses #103451\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPR #101210 migrated Codex app-server thread bindings from a JSON sidecar file (`<sessionFile>.codex-app-server.json`) into the `plugin_state_entries` SQLite table (plugin_id: `codex`, namespace: `app-server-thread-bindings`, entry_key: `session:main:<sessionId>`). The E2E release assertion script was not updated to match, so it reads from a file that no longer exists.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRelease maintainers running the `live-codex-npm-plugin` release-path lane will now correctly assert against the SQLite-backed binding store instead of hitting a missing-file error. No user-facing behavior change.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Replaced `readJson(bindingPath)` with `readCodexAppServerBindingFromPluginState(sessionId)` using `node:sqlite` DatabaseSync\n- The new function queries `plugin_state_entries` with the same plugin_id, namespace, and entry_key format used by the Codex plugin runtime\n- Lint passes on the changed file",
